# Lists on a card (decision 029): the wheel scrolls within what the scene
# says is possible, a provider can ask to keep a row in view, a row is picked
# up and carried only on the card that's shown, and an edit in place ends on Enter.

scenario: the wheel scrolls from what's shown, within bounds
start timer
click
wheel timer todos 0 30 100            -> scroll=timer/todos:30
wheel timer todos 30 500 100          -> scroll=timer/todos:100   # no further than the end
wheel timer todos 100 -400 100        -> scroll=timer/todos:0     # nor past the top

scenario: a reveal holds until the wheel takes over
start timer
click
reveal timer todos 7                  -> scroll=timer/todos:0+reveal
wheel timer todos 120 -40 200         -> scroll=timer/todos:80   # from what the reveal showed

scenario: a row is carried only on the card that's shown, and not under a dialog
start timer
pick timer todos 2 50                 -> carried=none            # not expanded
click
pick other todos 2 50                 -> carried=none            # not this card
pick timer todos 2 50                 -> carried=2
carry 90                              -> carried=2
put-down                              -> carried=none Expanded
pick timer todos 1 50
ask timer                             -> carried=none dialog=timer

scenario: the carried row goes with its card
start timer
start media
click
switch timer
pick timer todos 0 10                 -> carried=0
switch media                          -> carried=none

scenario: an edit starts with the text, and Enter ends it
start timer
click
edit timer todo.edit.3 Call           -> draft=Call
type mum                              -> draft=Callmum
submit                                -> draft=none Expanded     # a field would stay focused; an edit is done
focus timer todo.add
type next
submit                                -> draft=empty             # the add field keeps focus

scenario: a reveal can ask for the keyboard's focus, taken once (decision 063)
panel shelf keep
tile shelf                          -> Expanded expanded=shelf
reveal shelf items 0                -> focus=none
reveal shelf items 2 focus          -> focus=shelf/items/2
focus-taken                         -> focus=none

scenario: ...and it goes with its card
panel shelf keep
tile shelf
reveal shelf items 0 focus          -> focus=shelf/items/0
esc                                 -> focus=none
